# Build-context excludes for `-f server-rust/Dockerfile` (BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's file). The
# context is the repo root — this image needs `server-rust/`, `server/Migrations`,
# three SQL files under `infra/`, and LICENSE/NOTICE; everything else is weight.
#
# It is a superset of the repo-root `.dockerignore`, because when this file
# exists it REPLACES that one: every secret-bearing pattern there is repeated
# here. If a builder ignores per-Dockerfile ignore files, the root
# `.dockerignore` applies instead and the build still succeeds (larger context).

# --- never in any image context (mirrors the repo root .dockerignore) --------
.git
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
infra/prod/secrets.env
infra/prod/*.sops.env
infra/prod/*.plain.env
infra/prod/*.decrypted
infra/prod/age.key
infra/prod/keys.txt
**/*.secret.env
**/*.secrets.env
local-gate-evidence

# --- build output (server-rust/target alone is multi-GB) --------------------
target
**/target
.build
**/.build
**/.swiftpm
**/DerivedData
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__

# --- trees this image never copies ------------------------------------------
adapters
clients
# …except the canonical web client, which #1228 builds INTO this image (the
# `web-build` stage). A later pattern wins, so `clients` still excludes every
# other client tree — Swift, RN, the Tauri shell, web-legacy.
#
# **The whole of `clients/web` comes in, not a curated subset.** The first cut
# of this file also excluded `gates/`, `e2e/`, `scripts/` and `README.md`, on
# the reasoning that a production build never executes them — and the image
# then produced a DIFFERENT bundle than `npm run build` on the same commit
# (`index-VKgaCi6a.css` vs the host's `index-D9zcosSe.css`, and the entry chunk
# hash with it). Cause: Tailwind v4 has no content globs. `@import "tailwindcss"`
# (src/design/tokens.css:1) auto-detects by scanning the project's non-ignored
# files, so taking files OUT of the context takes utility classes OUT of the
# generated CSS. An image that builds a different artifact than the repo does
# is the exact drift this ticket exists to end, and ≈1.2MB of build context is
# not a price worth paying for it. Only build output and installed deps stay out.
!clients/web
clients/web/node_modules
clients/web/dist
clients/web/artifacts
docs
examples
fastlane
legal
relay
research
services
scripts
workers
server/Sources
server/Tests
server/Package.swift
server/Package.resolved
infra/eve
infra/workd
infra/prod/docker
BUILD_TICKETS.md
ROADMAP.md
STATUS.md
schema_v0.sql
